  "text": "library2 – The State University Of Zanzibar Skip to main content The State University Of Zanzibar Menu SUZIMS E-learning E-Office SMZ Mail Library ICT Center Staff Directory A – Z Policy Q.A The State University Of Zanzibar\t\t\t\t\t - SUZA Menu Home About Office Of Vice Chancellor List Of Vice Chancellor Vice Chancellor’s Message History And Facts About Us Campus Area Charter and Accrediation Vision Suza By Numbers Suza Anthem Organization And Governace Council Senate University Commitee University Acts Suza Organization Structure University Strategic Plan Policies, Regulation and Guidelines SUZASO University Leadership Chancelor Vice Chancelor Deputy VC Administration Deputy VC Academic University Administration Admission ADMISSION GUIDE BOOK Admission Information Undergraduate Programs PhD Programs Master Programs Diploma And Certificate Programs Kiswahili For Foreigners Short And Professional Courses Fee And Cost Academic Schools SCOPE SCCM SoE SoB SKFL Confucius Classroom SoA SNSS IoT IMS SHMS SoD Kigoda Centers ICT Center CDL TROCEN GCKSA Directorates DUS DGSRC Student Life Accomodation SUZASO Orientations Academic Calender Academic Advisors Alumni Research and Consultancy Find Researcher Research Areas Suza Google Scholar Research Facilities E-Services E-Office Utumishi SUZIMS Staff Mail SMZ Mail Google Apps My Courses / LMS Plagiarism Check E-Proz ZanVibali ERMS ZGAMIS Suza Forms Leaving Form Administration Form Academic Form Resert Password Form Innovation and Enterpreneurship Innovation Hubs WasteX Lab Suza Innovation Day Incubators Zatobi Remote Lab University Projects HEET Legacy of Zanzibar SUZA EXPANSION BSU SCCOPET Himili Pamoja PARTOMA MBD-Free RL4Eng RADIC Joint Marine EE-Shea CENSU Liverpool Pre-Vbd SAMAKI Geo-ICT EN-Suza BERT Collaboration Suza In Media Quick Links About Library Mission & Vission Services Objectives Rule & Ragulation E-Resources Staff HISTORICAL BACKGROUND The Library of the State University of Zanzibar was first established in 1979 as the library of the Institute of Kiswahili and Foreign Languages (IKFL). Following the establishment of the State University of Zanzibar (SUZA) under the Act No. 8 of 1999 of the Zanzibar House of Representatives and officially commenced to operate in 2002, the former IKFL library was phased out and became the State University of Zanzibar Library (SUZA Library). Currently, the Library is widened and spread its branches in Schools and Institute campuses as follows: the main library (Tunguu main campus), School of Kiswahili and Foreign Languages – SKFL (Nkrumah campus), School of Health and Medical Sciences (Mbweni campus), School of Business (Chwaka campus), Institute of Tourism (Maruhubi campus) , School of Agriculture ( Kizimbani Campus), School of Computing and Communication  Media  and in Pemba Island there is Benjamin William Mkapa library which is located at Mchangamdogo in Wete District. The Library collections cover the major disciplines such as  natural sciences, humanities and social sciences, computer sciences, education, health and medicine, business, accountancy, procurement, tourism, agriculture  and economic. The collection amounts about more than 50,000 books in both the main library and other branches in general. Mohamed Khamis Kombo Director of Library Services It is my pleasure to welcome you to the State University of Zanzibar Library. The library which support teachin… View Director Message Box 146, Tunguu, Zanzibar. +255 773 333 167 vc@suza.ac.tz Top Bar Menu SUZIMS E-learning E-Office SMZ Mail Library ICT Center Staff Directory A – Z Policy Q.A University School SCCM SKFL SNSS SoA SoB SoD SoE SHMS IoT SCOPE Other Resources WEMA MOE TCU COSTECH NECTA NACTE ZHESLB HESLB The website is Developed And Maintained By SUZA ICT - CENTER\n© Copyright 2026, All Rights Reserved",
